                <pb facs="0945" n="855" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg855"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.00/2150: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul in Chargé of the Legation in Honduras</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Lawton</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-01-15T17:00:00-05:48"><hi rendition="#italic">January 15,
                                1920—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 17—12:40
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>8. Hondurean Government reports that rumored revolutionary attempt from Nicaragua
                    has failed completely. The Nicaraguan President has denied all connection
                    therewith, acknowledging legality Hondurean elections and is apprehending
                    Honduras revolutionists.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lawton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
